{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.AlienBridgeEquation","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mathlib.AlienBridgeEquation","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.RingTheory.Derivation.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":22,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.AlienBridge.polyEulerSystem_alien_one_X_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.AlienBridge.polyEulerSystem_alien_one_X_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":260,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/AlienBridgeEquation.lean#L260-L266","doc":"The witness is genuinely nonzero: `Δ₁ X = X² ≠ 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.AlienBridge.polyEulerSystem_alien_one_X","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.AlienBridge.polyEulerSystem_alien_one_X","kind":"theorem","line":256,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/AlienBridgeEquation.lean#L256-L258","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.AlienBridge.polyEulerSystem","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.AlienBridge.polyEulerSystem","kind":"def","line":248,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/AlienBridgeEquation.lean#L248-L254","doc":"**A concrete inhabitant.**  `R[X]` with the Euler operator and `t = X`.\nIts `Δ₁` sends `X` to `X²`, which is nonzero for nontrivial `R` — so\n`BridgeSystem` has a model with nonzero weight and nonzero alien\nderivation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.AlienBridge.polyEuler_X","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.AlienBridge.polyEuler_X","kind":"theorem","line":242,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/AlienBridgeEquation.lean#L242-L246","doc":"The **Euler operator** `X·d/dX` on `R[X]` has `X` as an Euler coordinate. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.AlienBridge.polyDerivation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.AlienBridge.polyDerivation","kind":"def","line":231,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/AlienBridgeEquation.lean#L231-L240","doc":"Ordinary differentiation as a `Derivation` on `R[X]`.  Mathlib has\n`Polynomial.derivative` as a linear map and `derivative_mul` as the Leibniz\nrule, but does not package the two as a `Derivation`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.AlienBridge.eulerSystem_alien_one_self","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.AlienBridge.eulerSystem_alien_one_self","kind":"theorem","line":224,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/AlienBridgeEquation.lean#L224-L229","doc":"**The Euler system is non-trivial at weight 1.**  `Δ₁ t = t²`, so whenever\n`t² ≠ 0` the alien derivation at nonzero weight is nonzero.  This is the\nwitness that the theorems above are not vacuous. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.AlienBridge.eulerSystem_alien_apply","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.AlienBridge.eulerSystem_alien_apply","kind":"theorem","line":218,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/AlienBridgeEquation.lean#L218-L222","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.AlienBridge.eulerSystem","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.AlienBridge.eulerSystem","kind":"def","line":202,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/AlienBridgeEquation.lean#L202-L216","doc":"**The Euler bridge system.**  `Δ_n := tⁿ · D` with weight `n`, for any\nEuler coordinate `D t = t`.  The bridge equation holds *because* `D` scales\n`tⁿ` by `n`: differentiating past `tⁿ` produces exactly the `n · Δ_n` the\nrelation demands. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.AlienBridge.deriv_pow_eq_nsmul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.AlienBridge.deriv_pow_eq_nsmul","kind":"theorem","line":190,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/AlienBridgeEquation.lean#L190-L200","doc":"`D(tⁿ) = n · tⁿ` for an Euler coordinate `D t = t`.  The eigenvalue of `tⁿ`\nunder `D` is its degree, which is what makes the weights come out as `ℕ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.AlienBridge.BridgeSystem.ord_comm_of_weight_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.AlienBridge.BridgeSystem.ord_comm_of_weight_zero","kind":"theorem","line":162,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/AlienBridgeEquation.lean#L162-L169","doc":"**Weight zero is the degenerate case.**  At `weight ω = 0` the bridge\nequation says precisely that `Δ_ω` commutes with `∂` — the converse direction\nof `alien_eq_zero_of_ord_comm`, and a check that the sign and placement of the\nweight in the field are right. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.AlienBridge.BridgeSystem.ord_dotted_comm'","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.AlienBridge.BridgeSystem.ord_dotted_comm'","kind":"theorem","line":154,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/AlienBridgeEquation.lean#L154-L160","doc":"**The dotted derivative is exactly the correction term.**  Stated as the\nvanishing commutator, so the `= 0` shape is available for downstream Lie\narguments. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.AlienBridge.BridgeSystem.ord_dotted_comm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.AlienBridge.BridgeSystem.ord_dotted_comm","kind":"theorem","line":129,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/AlienBridgeEquation.lean#L129-L152","doc":"**The bridge proper: the dotted alien derivative commutes with `∂`.**\n\nLet `e_ω` be a formal exponential of weight `−ω`, i.e. `∂ e_ω = −ω · e_ω`\n(think `e^{−ωz}`), and set `Δ̇_ω f := e_ω · Δ_ω f`.  Then\n\n`∂ ∘ Δ̇_ω = Δ̇_ω ∘ ∂`.\n\nThe `ω` produced by the bridge equation is cancelled exactly by the `−ω` from\ndifferentiating `e_ω` — which is what the relation is *for*.  This is the\nstep that lets the `Δ_ω` be transported to the analytic side as ordinary\ncommuting operators.\n\n**Scope note.**  Unlike the other results here, this hypothesis is *not*\nwitnessed by `polyEulerSystem` below: `R[X]` has no element of `∂`-eigenvalue\n`−n`, since the Euler operator's eigenvalues on `R[X]` are the degrees `≥ 0`.\nA witness needs negative weights, i.e. Laurent polynomials `R[t, t⁻¹]` with\n`e = t^{−n}`.  That model is not built here, so the theorem is proved but its\nhypothesis is so far only exhibited abstractly. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.AlienBridge.BridgeSystem.weight_add_of_comp","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.AlienBridge.BridgeSystem.weight_add_of_comp","kind":"theorem","line":115,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/AlienBridgeEquation.lean#L115-L127","doc":"**Weights add under composition.**  Applying `Δ_ω'` then `Δ_ω` shifts by\n`ω + ω'`, so the alien derivations generate a weight-graded algebra rather\nthan an unstructured family.\n\nDerived from the bridge field twice plus `R`-linearity of `Δ_ω`; it is false\nwithout the field. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.AlienBridge.BridgeSystem.weight_shift","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.AlienBridge.BridgeSystem.weight_shift","kind":"theorem","line":104,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/AlienBridgeEquation.lean#L104-L113","doc":"**Weight shift.**  `Δ_ω` carries an `∂`-eigenvector of eigenvalue `λ` to an\n`∂`-eigenvector of eigenvalue `λ + ω`.\n\nThis is the structural reason alien derivatives detect instanton sectors: the\n`∂`-eigenvalue is the exponential weight `e^{λz}`, and `Δ_ω` steps it by\nexactly the Borel-singularity location `ω`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.AlienBridge.BridgeSystem.alien_eq_zero_of_ord_comm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.AlienBridge.BridgeSystem.alien_eq_zero_of_ord_comm","kind":"theorem","line":90,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/AlienBridgeEquation.lean#L90-L102","doc":"**The hypothesis has teeth.**  If `∂` commutes with `Δ_ω` and the weight acts\ninjectively (in particular, if `weight ω` is a non-zero-divisor and nonzero),\nthen `Δ_ω = 0`.\n\nSo the bridge equation is a genuine constraint, not bookkeeping: a system can\nsatisfy it with `Δ_ω ≠ 0` only by *failing* to commute, and by exactly the\namount `ω`.  Recorded because a structure field that any system satisfies\nwould make the theorems below vacuous. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.AlienBridge.BridgeSystem.ord_alien","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.AlienBridge.BridgeSystem.ord_alien","kind":"theorem","line":85,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/AlienBridgeEquation.lean#L85-L88","doc":"The bridge equation in solved form: `∂ ∘ Δ_ω = Δ_ω ∘ ∂ + ω · Δ_ω`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.AlienBridge.BridgeSystem.bridge","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.AlienBridge.BridgeSystem.bridge","kind":"theorem","line":78,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/AlienBridgeEquation.lean#L78-L78","doc":"**Écalle's bridge equation.**  `⁅∂, Δ_ω⁆ = ω · Δ_ω`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.AlienBridge.BridgeSystem.weight","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.AlienBridge.BridgeSystem.weight","kind":"def","line":76,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/AlienBridgeEquation.lean#L76-L76","doc":"The location of the singularity `ω`, as a scalar weight. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.AlienBridge.BridgeSystem.alien","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.AlienBridge.BridgeSystem.alien","kind":"def","line":74,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/AlienBridgeEquation.lean#L74-L74","doc":"The alien derivation at the singularity `ω`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.AlienBridge.BridgeSystem.ord","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.AlienBridge.BridgeSystem.ord","kind":"def","line":72,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/AlienBridgeEquation.lean#L72-L72","doc":"The ordinary derivation `∂`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.AlienBridge.BridgeSystem.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.AlienBridge.BridgeSystem.mk","kind":"ctor","line":69,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/AlienBridgeEquation.lean#L69-L69","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.AlienBridge.BridgeSystem","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.AlienBridge.BridgeSystem","kind":"structure","line":60,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/AlienBridgeEquation.lean#L60-L79","doc":"An **alien derivation system carrying Écalle's bridge equation**: an ordinary\nderivation `∂`, a family of alien derivations `Δ_ω` indexed by `Ω`, a weight\n`ω ↦ weight ω ∈ R` recording each singularity's location, and the relation\n\n`∂(Δ_ω f) − Δ_ω(∂ f) = weight ω • Δ_ω f`.\n\nThe relation is a **field**, i.e. a hypothesis on the system.  It is not\nderived from the other data and is not claimed of any particular analytic\nconstruction. ","signatureChunk":0}]}